- label: bunfig.toml contains no [jsx] section (Cargo-Cult unused runtime config copied from templates; the file-local /** jsx */ and /** Fragment */ pragmas in src/layout.tsx plus import from "hono/jsx" suffice for classic JSX transform under Bun direct .ts runs) (verifiable by: ! test -f bunfig.toml || ! grep -q '^\[jsx\]' bunfig.toml )
  command: test ! -f bunfig.toml || ! grep -q '^\[jsx\]' bunfig.toml
  tags: [jsx, jsxFrag, implemented]
- package.json contains no "type": "module" field (Cargo-Cult unused config copied from node/TS templates; never exercised by the project's actual runtime paths: bun direct .ts execution, "bun run" package scripts, Dockerfile which COPYs package.json then bun install --production then later src/ and uses direct bun ENTRYPOINT on cli.ts with no tsc dist step; verifiable by: ! grep -q "\"type\": \"module\"" package.json ) @implemented
- README.md "With a preset" section no longer duplicates the `--preset tech-news` (or `-P ml-ai`) + `pace --list-presets` example phrasing from the "## Presets" section; instead uses a concise cross-reference to "## Presets" (or `pace --list-presets`) while preserving how-to guidance and all info; the "## Presets" section keeps the full description and table (verifiable by: ! grep -A8 '### With a preset' README.md | grep -q 'append `--preset tech-news\'' && grep -q 'See the "## Presets" section' README.md && grep -q 'Presets are bundled in the Docker image and selectable with a single flag (`--preset tech-news` or `-P ml-ai`; see `pace --list-presets`)' README.md ) @implemented
- label: skills/pace-config/SKILL.md Transform reference contains no verbosity-inflating restating per-transform comments (the '# Keep the N most recent items' before obvious 'type: latest' and '# Add LLM-generated summaries' before 'type: llm-summarize' have been removed; type: key + example params + section prose are self-documenting); verifiable by: ! grep -q '^ # Keep the N most recent items' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md && ! grep -q '^ # Add LLM-generated summaries' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md
  command:  ! grep -q "^  # Keep the N most recent items" skills/pace-config/SKILL.md && ! grep -q "^  # Add LLM-generated summaries" skills/pace-config/SKILL.md 
  tags: [implemented]
- label: skills/pace-config/SKILL.md frontmatter contains no 'compatibility:' key (Cargo-Cult unreferenced/parsed frontmatter field present only in the 2 SKILL.md files themselves and nowhere referenced/parsed in project code, docs, configs or skill consumers; rotate after verbosity nwf in same file) (verifiable by: ! grep -q '^compatibility:' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md && grep -c '^compatibility:' skills/pace-*/SKILL.md | grep -q ':1$')
  command: ! grep -q '^compatibility:' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md
  tags: [implemented]
- skills/pace-config/SKILL.md Transform reference yaml contains no verbosity-inflating restating per-transform comments (the '# Deduplicate items' before obvious 'type: dedupe' and '# Group related items (no LLM)' before 'type: cluster' have been removed; type: key + params + section prose are self-documenting, similar to nwf); verifiable by: ! grep -q ' # Deduplicate items' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md && ! grep -q ' # Group related items (no LLM)' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md @implemented
- skills/pace-config/SKILL.md Transform reference yaml contains no verbosity-inflating restating per-transform comments (the '# Keep items matching LLM-evaluated criteria' before obvious 'type: llm-filter' and '# Reorder by LLM-scored relevance to user interests' before 'type: llm-rank' have been removed; type: key + params + section prose are self-documenting, similar to nwf/evu); verifiable by: ! grep -q ' # Keep items matching LLM-evaluated criteria' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md && ! grep -q ' # Reorder by LLM-scored relevance to user interests' skills/pace-config/SKILL.md @implemented

# examples
- label: The examples/ directory contains curated example configs that are valid and have screenshots
  command: set -e; for cfg in examples/*.yaml; do name="${cfg%.yaml}"; [ -f "${name}.png" ] || { echo "missing screenshot for $cfg"; exit 1; }; bun run src/cli.ts config check "$cfg" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "config check failed for $cfg"; exit 1; }; done
  tags: [implemented]

# layout
- label: flex:0 layout nodes get height:auto so they shrink to content instead of claiming the parent's full height
  command: grep -q "flex:none; height:auto;" src/layout/flex-styles.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: Responsive media widgets remain usable across viewport sizes: desktop image and iframe flex items are capped at 70vh so tall media cannot collapse following panels, while phone layouts render images at intrinsic aspect ratio, remove the desktop cap, retain configured iframe height, and keep following content page-scrollable
  command: bun test src/media-widget-responsive.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented, responsive-media]

# sharing
- label: pace share export --single-file writes one self-contained index.html with bundled CSS inlined and no stylesheet dependency, while default export remains the compatible index.html plus styles.css pair
  command: bun test src/share-export.test.ts src/cli-share.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'single-file'
  tags: [spec, implemented, single-file-share]

## static-dashboards
- Publishing a Static Dashboard does not require the user to expose or operate a public pace web server @implemented
- A Static Dashboard export includes a rendered index.html file and the required CSS needed to view the snapshot later @implemented
- A user can publish the current Dashboard snapshot to a configured Share Storage Backend from the CLI @implemented
- Static Dashboard artifacts never include adapter credentials, LLM API keys, auth tokens, or unresolved environment variable placeholders @implemented
- Publishing a Static Dashboard reports the storage backend name and browser-rendered share URL on success, and errors start with 'share:' on failure @implemented
- Static Dashboards are read-only: refresh controls, forms, and routes that require a running pace server are omitted or rendered inert in the exported artifact @implemented
- Static Dashboard export can write to a local directory without using a remote Share Backend, so users can inspect the artifact before publishing @implemented
- The CLI exposes pace share export [dir] and pace share gist; share export supports output directories, share gist supports renderer URL, gist ID updates, and visibility, and both commands route failures through share: errors @implemented
- label: Static Dashboard snapshots render item timestamps and panel refresh timestamps as stable absolute UTC values instead of frozen relative ages; interactive Dashboards retain relative ages
  command: bun test src/share-export.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'renders stable absolute UTC timestamps instead of frozen relative ages'
  tags: [spec, implemented, static-absolute-time]
- label: Static Dashboard exports render iframe Widgets as non-fetching placeholders that explain live embedded content is not included and provide a safe explicit source link; interactive Dashboards continue rendering the sandboxed iframe
  command: bun test src/share-export.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'replaces live iframe with an offline-safe source link'
  tags: [spec, implemented, offline-iframe-placeholder]
- label: Static Dashboard exports render remote image Widgets as non-fetching placeholders that preserve meaningful alt context and provide an explicit safe link; interactive Dashboards continue rendering the configured image and link
  command: bun test src/share-export.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'replaces remote image with an offline-safe contextual link'
  tags: [spec, implemented, offline-image-placeholder]
- label: Static Dashboard exports replace remote images inside Markdown or HTML Text Widgets with visible non-fetching omission text that preserves meaningful alt context; interactive Dashboards continue rendering the sanitized images
  command: bun test src/share-export.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'replaces rich-text images with offline alt context'
  tags: [spec, implemented, offline-rich-text-images]

## backends
- The GitHub Gist Share Storage Backend stores Static Dashboard artifacts in a public or secret gist using a GitHub token supplied by the user's environment @implemented
- Share Storage Backends support creating a new shared snapshot and updating a previously published snapshot so the Share Renderer URL remains stable when the backend supports stable artifact IDs @implemented
- Share Storage Backend configuration is separate from content adapters so publishing settings do not affect dashboard refresh behavior @implemented
- Secret Gist publishing is unlisted but not private; anyone with the returned share URL can view the Static Dashboard @implemented
- When publishing through the GitHub Gist Share Storage Backend, pace returns a browser-rendered Share Renderer URL by default rather than the raw gist URL @implemented
- gisthost.github.io is the default Share Renderer for GitHub Gist publishing, and users can configure a different compatible renderer @implemented

# docs

## readme
- label: README.md leads with a concise product promise, immediate visual proof, fast copy-paste start paths, and static sharing commands without repeating demo calls to action
  command: grep -q "^# pace$" README.md && grep -q "self-hosted dashboard" README.md && grep -q "## Get Started" README.md && grep -q "## Share a Snapshot" README.md && grep -q "pace share gist" README.md && [ $(grep -ci "click the thumbnail" README.md) -eq 0 ]
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: README.md places Preset showcase immediately after Why Pace and before Get Started, keeps it in the same thumbnail-grid style as Example Dashboards, keeps Example Dashboards secondary, and presents agent skills as the primary setup path before Docker or source commands
  command: python3 -c "from pathlib import Path; t=Path('README.md').read_text(); lines=t.splitlines(); pos=lambda s: next((i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.strip()==s), 999999); assert pos('## Why Pace') < pos('## Presets') < pos('#### Preset showcase') < pos('## Get Started') < pos('## Example Dashboards'); assert pos('## Built-in content adapters') < pos('## Example Dashboards'); assert t.count('| | | | |') >= 2; assert '[![Tech News preset](./assets/preset-tech-news.png)](./presets/config.tech-news.yaml)' in t; assert t.count('./presets/config.tech-news.yaml') >= 2; assert 'reference dashboards' in t; assert 'Recommended: agent skills' in t; assert pos('### Recommended: agent skills') < pos('### Secondary: Docker'); assert pos('### Recommended: agent skills') < pos('### Secondary: from source')"
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: README.md describes Pace in plain concrete language: self-hosted dashboard, YAML config, Bun or Docker runtime, optional LLM transforms, and no hype phrases like revolutionary, game-changing, internet you actually follow, or noisy sources
  command: grep -q 'self-hosted dashboard' README.md && grep -q 'YAML' README.md && grep -q 'Bun process or Docker container' README.md && grep -q 'optional' README.md && ! grep -Ei '\b(revolutionary|game-changing|next-generation|supercharge|unlock|internet you actually follow|noisy sources|dashboard you own)\b' README.md
  tags: [spec, implemented]

# static-dashboards
- label: Large static snapshots mark their document mode and use browser-native off-screen panel rendering containment, keeping every panel and item in the portable HTML while avoiding initial layout and paint work for panels outside the viewport
  command: bun test src/share-export.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'contains off-screen panels without dropping snapshot content'
  tags: [spec, implemented, large-static-rendering]

# security
- label: Diagnostic errors redact credential-like URL fragment values before they reach logs, health responses, or refresh responses
  command: bun test src/url-credential-diagnostics.test.ts
  tags: [spec, pace-use-case-url-fragment-redaction, implemented]

# transforms

## llm
- label: When optional LLM full-text enrichment is unavailable for pending items, Pace logs one credential-free aggregate warning and continues summarizing from available item metadata
  command: bun test src/fetch-content.test.ts
  tags: [spec, pace-use-case-content-enrichment-diagnostics, implemented]
- label: LLM completion diagnostics classify provider response failures by actionable HTTP status without logging provider-controlled error text, and report responses containing no text
  command: bun test src/llm.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'provider response diagnostics'
  tags: [spec, pace-use-case-safe-llm-provider-errors, implemented]
- label: Every LLM completion created from Pace configuration uses that configuration api_key explicitly, including custom OpenAI-compatible providers without provider environment variables
  command: bun test src/llm.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'configured API key'
  tags: [spec, pace-use-case-custom-provider-api-key, implemented]
